    How many apps does it take to run a creative agency? Depends what you need to do. Find clients, manage projects, talk to clients, get designs approved, chase payments. So a lot of apps. Way too many. Where are your leads? A CRM. Projects. A project management tool. Feedback. Email and a separate proofing app. Client conversations. Somewhere else. Proposals, invoices, payments. More tools and none of them seem to know what's happening in the others. What if they were all connected? Meet Nod Stage. One connected workspace built around how creative studios actually work. Okay, where do I start? With your leads, inquiries, discovery calls, follow -ups and proposals in one pipeline. And when a deal is won? It becomes a project, tasks, deadlines and your team's workload. What about the client? They get their own branded portal. They review proofs, leave visual feedback and approve. And revisions? Managed right there, extra work becomes a change order. Then I still need an invoicing app. No invoices and payments live here too. So do your calendar, video messages, forms, templates and automations. And testimonials. Requested when the client approves. So I don't need to keep jumping between all those tools. That's the whole point. Less switching, less chasing. And it's free to start. Free to start, sign up at nodstage .com.
